@* Blazor Server reconnection UI.

   The framework watches for an element with id "components-reconnect-modal" and, when the
   SignalR circuit drops, toggles one of these classes on it:

     components-reconnect-show     – connection lost, actively retrying
     components-reconnect-hide     – reconnected / normal
     components-reconnect-failed   – automatic retries were exhausted
     components-reconnect-rejected – the server already discarded the circuit (reload required)

   The CSS in ReconnectModal.razor.css shows the matching message for each state.
   wwwroot/reconnect.js adds auto-retry (on "failed") and auto-reload (on "rejected"). *@

<div id="components-reconnect-modal" class="components-reconnect-hide">
    <div class="reconnect-dialog">
        <div class="reconnect-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        <div class="reconnect-message reconnect-show-message">
            <h3>Reconnecting&hellip;</h3>
            <p>
                The connection to the server was lost. Trying to reconnect
                <span class="reconnect-attempt">
                    (attempt <span id="components-reconnect-current-attempt"></span>
                    of <span id="components-reconnect-max-retries"></span>)
                </span>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reconnect-message reconnect-failed-message">
            <h3>Reconnecting&hellip;</h3>
            <p>The connection dropped. Still trying to get you back&hellip;</p>
            <button type="button" onclick="window.Blazor.reconnect()">Retry now</button>
        </div>

        <div class="reconnect-message reconnect-rejected-message">
            <h3>Connection lost</h3>
            <p>Couldn&rsquo;t reconnect to the server. Reloading the page&hellip;</p>
            <button type="button" onclick="location.reload()">Reload now</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
